From 1ba8227bb9ea50d7a5629ea0cc15f9fcdf00b348 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 06:59:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][PlayerInfo] The sentence says frames lost only when
 the loss is sustained, and by its cause

The overview of the player information said "everything as intended"
while Kodi dropped or skipped frames all along (a report showed 4
dropped and 8 skipped every 10 seconds at 59.94 Hz), and its rows of
dropped and skipped frames count from the start of the video, so a
seek or a start that lost a few frames by design looked the same as a
PC that cannot keep up.

Kodi loses frames by design around a start, a seek or a chapter jump,
a pause and its resume, a change of refresh rate or of stream, and
while its cache refills. None of that is a fault, and a sentence that
named it would blame the PC for what the network or a seek did. So
CLostFrames (HadesPlayerInfo.h) counts the frames that Kodi's video
player dropped and its renderer skipped (CDataCacheCore) only in
steady playback: for 5 s after a new output of a video, an emptying of
the renderer's queue (seeks, chapters, changes of stream), or any
moment paused, at another speed or seeking, nothing is counted; what
is lost while the player buffers is counted apart. Samples after a
gap (the page was closed) or with counters that went back (another
video) start again.

The sentence changes only on sustained loss: at least 6 frames over
the last 30 s, lost in at least two of its three parts of 10 s, so a
one-off burst never flips it; the case of the report is past both in
its second part. It then names the cause where one can be seen: the
graphics busy (from 90 %, said with the percent), else how many frames
were dropped or came too late, the larger first. A display rate that
does not fit the video keeps its own sentence, since its cadence skips
frames by itself. Frames lost while the stream buffers are a note:
the network or the source, not the PC. With no frame lost, the
sentence is what it was, and the rows of dropped and skipped frames
stay as they are.

New strings in English and in the three Spanish ones. Host tests
(tools/regress of LibreELEC, kodi-host ux: verdict_test.cpp,
lost_frames_src.py, check_verdict_test.py).
